think REMEMBER.md (git nib 315c2d2d0b) is stale against HEAD 39203ca — the bench has climbed far past it into Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium); trusted the code and git log over the card.
think The whole-road Lindy-first crux is the current journey's next rung, not a fixed-itinerary rung: HEAD landed Portage r2 (atomic), so the next agent-doable crux is Portage r3 — the crossing travels as text.
think Modeled the rung on the family's own `_bron` idiom (freight_bron.rye the closest kin): a fixed-order line-per-field record, a purpose-built bounded hex/decimal reader, render/parse a fixed point, a seen-bitmask refusing MissingField.
think The record's fields: id · from · to-world · to-account · amount · digest · out-head · in-head (the exploration's own list). from/to/world/id/digest/heads render as fixed-width hex, amount as decimal.
think The crux is acceptance BY THE RECORD ALONE — designed two teeth: self_certifies re-derives the digest from the record's own bound fields (id·amount·from·world·to) so any altered field diverges; accept ties the light record to r1's heavy proof — out-head must equal World A's real order-head with a matching burn, in-head must equal World B's real order-head crediting the recipient under this digest (resolve_world refuses NoMatchingBurn otherwise).
obs GREEN after one shadow fix (a local hex buffer named from_hex shadowed the from_hex fn — renamed to from_hex_buf); no logic red. Conservation across the pair read from the record's own worlds (40 left A == 40 reached B).
obs Tamper teeth all bite: a changed amount breaks self-certification (NotSelfCertified), a changed out-head refuses OutHeadMismatch, a changed in-head refuses InHeadMismatch; every malformed record (bad header · unknown field · bad line · bad hex · bad amount · missing field) refuses.
obs Composes portage + cord + voucher + kumara public API only, editing none; Portage r1 crux and r2 atomic law both re-run GREEN at the witness door; demo world/keeper seeds — no key, no funds, no network, no value crossed; a served crossing (World B fetching World A's record over Comlink) stays the Comlink-served custody gate.
